body:
We have different APIS with similar numeric refinements:

numericSelector:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.numericSelector({
    container: '#popularity-selector',
    attributeName: 'popularity',
    operator: '>=',
    options: [
      {label: 'Top 10', value: 9900},
      {label: 'Top 100', value: 9800},
      {label: 'Top 500', value: 9700}
    ]
  })
);
```

numericRefinementList:

```js
search.addWidget(
  instantsearch.widgets.numericRefinementList({
    container: '#popularity',
    attributeName: 'popularity',
    options: [
      {name: 'All'},
      {end: 4, name: 'less than 4'},
      {start: 4, end: 4, name: '4'},
      {start: 5, end: 10, name: 'between 5 and 10'},
      {start: 10, name: 'more than 10'}
    ],
    templates: {
      header: 'Price'
    }
  })
);
```

Issues:

* numericSelector allows all helper operators but you can't do "BETWEEN"
* numericRefinementList allows BETWEEN but you don't know if `end` and `start` are inclusive or exclusive.

Correct me if I am wrong.

Can we make this more consistent?
